WEBVTT

00:01.560 --> 00:05.640
[baby crying]

00:05.680 --> 00:07.640
Hurry, or they'll kill us all!

00:08.160 --> 00:09.200
Hurry!

00:12.320 --> 00:13.880
Do your breasts still give milk?

00:13.960 --> 00:16.160
Where are you going?

00:16.239 --> 00:17.800
They have asked for her.

01:24.400 --> 01:26.160
Sir? This is her.

01:27.800 --> 01:29.560
The girl who tells fortunes?

01:43.840 --> 01:46.440
[chanting softly in foreign language]

01:58.000 --> 01:59.560
[horse neighs]

02:02.360 --> 02:05.800
They're doing a magic spell
to make it win a race.

02:12.680 --> 02:14.960
The horse's name
is Meaghan Boy.

02:15.040 --> 02:17.560
Kemp ton, 3:00, Monday.

02:17.640 --> 02:21.120
You ladies have a bet yourselves
but don't tell anyone else.

02:26.960 --> 02:30.440
[theme song playing]

02:46.040 --> 02:49.320
[preacher] ...and Abraham
made his home in a cave,

02:49.400 --> 02:54.080
but it was good because God
resided there with him.

02:54.160 --> 02:57.120
You see, children, God does not care

02:57.200 --> 03:00.880
if you live in a slum
or in a mansion.

03:00.960 --> 03:05.360
God does not care
if you are rich or you are poor.

03:05.440 --> 03:07.800
You are still...

03:13.920 --> 03:15.120
Morning, sir.

03:24.440 --> 03:26.680
[policeman] Good morning,
Mr. Shelby.

04:05.440 --> 04:07.280
[children laughing, chattering]

04:09.560 --> 04:10.840
[man 1] Come on, lad.

04:11.840 --> 04:13.520
[man 2] Morning, Mr. Shelby.

04:13.600 --> 04:15.160
[man 1] Come on, hurry up!

04:30.440 --> 04:31.720
[Thomas] Finn?

04:34.200 --> 04:35.920
Arthur's mad as hell.

04:37.240 --> 04:38.360
[sighs]

04:39.800 --> 04:42.400
What does a ten-year-old
know about hell, eh?

04:42.480 --> 04:44.000
I'm 11 Sunday.

04:52.560 --> 04:55.640
[all chattering]

05:17.840 --> 05:19.440
[man] Get your bets in now.

05:26.040 --> 05:29.320
[John] Tommy! Tommy!
Tommy, look at the book.

05:29.400 --> 05:30.760
- Just look.
- Tommy!

05:30.840 --> 05:33.200
- All on Meaghan Boy.
- Good work, John.

05:33.280 --> 05:34.480
Tommy!

05:34.560 --> 05:36.760
Get in here, now!

05:37.360 --> 05:41.240
That'll be six pennies, Nipper.
That's ten bob you'll see for that.

05:49.800 --> 05:52.400
You was seen
doing the powder trick

05:52.480 --> 05:54.360
down at Garrison Courts.

05:55.000 --> 05:56.640
Times are hard.

05:56.920 --> 05:59.040
People need a reason
to lay a bet.

05:59.200 --> 06:01.000
There was a Chinese.

06:01.080 --> 06:03.400
The washer women say
she's a witch.

06:03.960 --> 06:05.360
It helps them believe.

06:05.440 --> 06:07.280
We don't mess with Chinese.

06:07.360 --> 06:11.880
- Look at the book--
- Chinese have cutters of their own.

06:11.960 --> 06:13.480
We agreed, Arthur.

06:14.240 --> 06:16.960
I'm taking charge of
drumming up new money.

06:19.480 --> 06:21.480
What if Meaghan Boy
wins, Tommy?

06:22.360 --> 06:24.280
You fixing races now?

06:24.360 --> 06:28.720
Do you have permission from Billy Kimber
to be fixing races, mm?

06:29.720 --> 06:31.760
What's got into you?

06:32.520 --> 06:37.120
You think we can take on
the Chinese and Billy Kimber.

06:37.200 --> 06:41.680
- Billy's got a bloody army--
- I think, Arthur.

06:42.240 --> 06:43.840
That's what I do.

06:47.280 --> 06:48.680
I think.

06:49.880 --> 06:52.120
So that you don't have to.

06:56.040 --> 06:57.760
There's news from Belfast.

07:03.600 --> 07:06.600
I'm calling a family council
tonight at 8:00.

07:06.680 --> 07:08.280
I want all of us there.

07:08.840 --> 07:10.320
You hear me?

07:10.400 --> 07:12.080
There's trouble coming.

07:12.160 --> 07:13.800
[train whistle blowing]

07:57.840 --> 07:59.520
[train whistle blowing]

08:02.480 --> 08:04.720
[crowd cheering]

08:11.440 --> 08:13.680
All right, shut up now.
Shut up.

08:15.760 --> 08:20.080
Comrades, we're here today
to take a vote on strike action.

08:20.160 --> 08:21.600
[crowd] Yes!

08:22.200 --> 08:24.800
But before we have
a show of hands for that,

08:25.000 --> 08:28.680
let's have a show of hands
from all those who fought in France.

08:28.760 --> 08:31.760
All those who stood side by side
with your comrades

08:31.840 --> 08:33.880
and watched your comrades fall.

08:34.360 --> 08:35.679
Raise your hands.

08:40.159 --> 08:43.440
The blood shed on Flanders Fields,

08:43.799 --> 08:46.000
the sweat of your brows...

08:46.920 --> 08:49.160
Who reaps the rewards?

08:49.240 --> 08:51.640
- Is it you?
- [crowd] No!

08:51.720 --> 08:54.040
- Is it your wives?
- No!

08:54.120 --> 08:57.040
- Who, then, do they stand among us?
- No!

08:57.120 --> 09:01.000
Or do they sit at home
comfortable with a full belly

09:01.080 --> 09:05.120
while you scrape to find enough
to put shoes on your children's feet!

09:05.200 --> 09:06.240
[crowd] Yes!

09:06.320 --> 09:10.000
And what is the reward they offer you
for your sacrifices made?

09:10.480 --> 09:12.920
A fucking cut in your wages.

09:13.000 --> 09:14.840
That is your reward.

09:15.200 --> 09:17.680
Raise a hand,
all those who want to strike.

09:17.760 --> 09:19.280
[all] Yes!

09:41.520 --> 09:43.440
[train whistle blowing]

10:12.840 --> 10:14.400
On the house, Mr. Shelby.

10:35.040 --> 10:37.120
- I'll take a Mild.
- [Harry] Right.

10:56.840 --> 11:00.080
Cheers, Thomas,
good health to you.

11:06.240 --> 11:08.080
The crown of a prince.

11:11.400 --> 11:12.920
Soon to be king, I'd bet.

11:13.000 --> 11:14.280
You don't bet.

11:14.640 --> 11:17.960
No, but these past few days
I've been speculating.

11:21.640 --> 11:22.920
About what?

11:23.760 --> 11:26.000
One of my Union comrades
has a sister

11:26.080 --> 11:29.200
who works in the telegraph office
at the BSA factory.

11:29.280 --> 11:32.760
She says, over the past week
they've had messages coming up

11:32.840 --> 11:36.160
from London to the brass,
from Winston Churchill himself.

11:40.960 --> 11:42.640
Something about a robbery.

11:43.840 --> 11:46.560
"A robbery of national
significance," it said.

11:49.120 --> 11:52.840
She found a list of names
left on the telegraph machine.

11:54.640 --> 11:57.960
And on that list was your name
and my name together.

12:00.440 --> 12:03.560
What kind of a list would have
the name of a communist

12:03.640 --> 12:06.040
and the name of a bookmaker
side by side?

12:09.000 --> 12:12.800
Perhaps it's a list of men
who give false hope to the poor.

12:13.960 --> 12:16.720
The only difference
between you and me, Freddie,

12:16.800 --> 12:20.400
is that sometimes my horses
stand a chance of winning.

12:28.200 --> 12:32.200
You know, there are days when I hear
about the cuttings and beatings

12:32.280 --> 12:35.640
that I really wish I'd let you
take that bullet in France.

12:36.320 --> 12:39.440
Believe me, there are nights
I wish you had.

12:39.520 --> 12:41.000
[door slams open]

12:41.080 --> 12:42.520
[glass breaking]

12:42.600 --> 12:43.640
Hey!

12:47.880 --> 12:50.120
- They're going to get me!
- On three.

12:50.200 --> 12:53.200
- They are going to get me!
- One, two, three, down!

12:53.280 --> 12:56.360
- Breathe, Danny, breathe.
- They're going to get me!

12:56.440 --> 12:57.960
They're going to get me!

12:58.040 --> 13:01.120
Danny. Danny.
Danny, you're home.

13:01.200 --> 13:04.400
We're all home in England.
You are not in France.

13:04.480 --> 13:07.480
You're not an artillery shell,
Danny, you're a man.

13:07.560 --> 13:08.800
Hey?

13:08.880 --> 13:11.960
You're not a whiz-bang.
You're a human being, Danny.

13:12.040 --> 13:13.600
You're all right.

13:13.680 --> 13:15.160
You're all right.

13:15.240 --> 13:16.480
You're all right.

13:16.840 --> 13:18.520
Up! Up!

13:22.360 --> 13:24.000
It's all right.

13:24.360 --> 13:25.680
It's all right.

13:28.440 --> 13:29.920
Ah! Hell!

13:30.000 --> 13:31.560
Did I do it again?

13:32.840 --> 13:34.280
You did it again, Danny.

13:34.360 --> 13:37.000
[crying]

13:37.880 --> 13:39.800
You got to stop doing this, man.

13:40.440 --> 13:43.400
- It's all right.
- Oh, God! Mr. Shelby, I'm sorry.

13:43.480 --> 13:46.520
It's all right. You go home
to your wife now, Danny.

13:46.600 --> 13:49.880
Try and get all that smoke
and mud out of your head, eh?

13:49.960 --> 13:51.720
Yes, Mr. Shelby. I'm sorry.

13:53.160 --> 13:54.440
Go on.

13:58.560 --> 14:01.320
Mr. Shelby, you have to
do something about him.

14:01.400 --> 14:02.480
Damn right, Harry.

14:02.560 --> 14:05.880
You pay the Peaky Blinders
a lot of money for protection.

14:06.360 --> 14:09.280
You're the law around here now,
Tommy, aren't you?

14:09.360 --> 14:12.640
Maybe you should put a bullet
in Danny Whiz-Bang's head

14:12.720 --> 14:14.480
like they do with mad horses.

14:16.040 --> 14:19.440
Maybe you'll have to put a bullet
in my head someday, too.

14:29.400 --> 14:31.560
Bring the bill to
the Peaky Blinders.

14:31.640 --> 14:33.000
We'll take care of it.

14:52.680 --> 14:54.200
Look at the gun.

14:55.680 --> 14:57.120
You recognize it?

14:57.360 --> 14:58.400
Mmm.

14:59.440 --> 15:00.480
[screams]

15:00.560 --> 15:02.720
Get up off your ass,
you umping pig.

15:02.800 --> 15:05.440
Aunt Poll! What the fuck
did you do that for?

15:05.520 --> 15:08.640
Finn was playing with this,
this afternoon by the Cut.

15:08.720 --> 15:11.160
It was loaded.
Nearly blew Ada's tits off.

15:11.240 --> 15:13.160
It must've fell out
of my pocket.

15:13.240 --> 15:15.320
He said he found it
on the sideboard

15:15.400 --> 15:17.720
of the betting shop,
with bullets in it.

15:18.200 --> 15:19.880
I... I must have been drunk.

15:21.560 --> 15:23.000
When are you not drunk?

15:23.080 --> 15:25.120
Look, Aunt Pol. I'm sorry.

15:25.680 --> 15:27.800
I'm... I'm sorry.

15:28.880 --> 15:30.880
Keep this
between ourselves,

15:30.960 --> 15:33.520
if you swear not to leave
guns lying around.

15:36.960 --> 15:40.080
Look, I know having four kids
without a woman is hard,

15:40.160 --> 15:42.880
but my boot is harder.
Now come on, we're late.

15:43.920 --> 15:46.680
[Arthur] Right, I've called
this family meeting

15:46.760 --> 15:49.160
because I've got some
very important news.

15:49.680 --> 15:53.000
Scud boat and Love lock got back
from Belfast last night.

15:53.720 --> 15:56.600
They were buying a stallion
to cover their mares.

15:56.840 --> 15:59.720
They were in a pub on
Shank hill Road yesterday

15:59.800 --> 16:02.720
and in that pub
there was a copper,

16:03.360 --> 16:04.960
handing out these.

16:07.920 --> 16:11.480
"If you're over five feet and can fight,
come to Birmingham."

16:12.360 --> 16:16.680
They're recruiting Protestant Irishmen
to come over here as Specials.

16:16.760 --> 16:19.720
- To do what?
- [Thomas] To clean up the city, Ada.

16:19.800 --> 16:21.520
He's the Chief Inspector.

16:22.240 --> 16:25.960
The last four years he's been
clearing the IRA out of Belfast.

16:26.160 --> 16:28.120
How do you know so bloody much?

16:28.200 --> 16:30.640
'Cause I asked the coppers
on our payroll.

16:30.720 --> 16:32.200
Why didn't you tell me?

16:34.280 --> 16:35.840
I'm telling you.

16:37.920 --> 16:40.000
Why send him to Birmingham?

16:40.120 --> 16:42.600
There's been all these
strikes at the BSA,

16:42.680 --> 16:44.360
and the Austin works lately.

16:44.800 --> 16:48.480
Now the papers are talking
about sedition. And revolution.

16:49.240 --> 16:51.320
I reckon it's communists
he's after.

16:51.400 --> 16:54.080
So this copper is gonna
leave us alone, right?

16:54.160 --> 16:58.360
There are Irishmen in Green Lanes
who left Belfast to get away from him.

16:58.440 --> 17:01.240
Catholic men who crossed him
used to disappear.

17:01.320 --> 17:05.680
Yeah, but we ain't IRA.
We bloody fought for the King.

17:05.760 --> 17:07.520
Anyway, we're Peaky Blinders.

17:07.599 --> 17:10.160
- We're not scared of coppers.
- He's right.

17:10.240 --> 17:13.079
If they come for us,
we'll cut them a smile each.

17:13.160 --> 17:14.920
So, Arthur, is that it?

17:15.880 --> 17:18.000
[Arthur] What do you think,
Aunt Pol?

17:18.079 --> 17:20.079
This family does everything open.

17:21.040 --> 17:24.079
You have nothing more to say
to this meeting, Thomas?

17:24.160 --> 17:25.240
No.

17:25.319 --> 17:27.240
Nothing that's women's business.

17:27.319 --> 17:30.200
This whole bloody enterprise
was women's business

17:30.280 --> 17:32.120
while you boys
were away at war.

17:32.200 --> 17:33.360
What's changed?

17:34.440 --> 17:35.720
We came back.

17:36.360 --> 17:41.240
And the Lord will smite the unholy
when the great judgment comes.

17:41.320 --> 17:43.720
And judgment is coming, my friends.

17:43.800 --> 17:46.960
Judgment is coming
to this wicked city.

17:47.040 --> 17:49.920
And your wickedness and your fornication

17:50.000 --> 17:51.880
will be revealed.

17:51.960 --> 17:54.880
You cannot hide
from the Creator.

17:54.960 --> 17:58.920
You cannot hide from
the Almighty himself.

17:59.000 --> 18:01.120
The Creator sees all.

18:01.200 --> 18:04.680
You cannot hide
from the true and living God.

18:04.760 --> 18:06.240
[man] Get out of here!

18:16.080 --> 18:17.560
Fuck off!

18:29.160 --> 18:30.840
[woman] Go away!

18:30.920 --> 18:32.960
That's it, I don't go any further.

18:48.600 --> 18:49.920
[sighs]

18:50.000 --> 18:52.160
I have ten minutes.
What do you want?

18:57.200 --> 18:58.680
An explanation.

19:02.400 --> 19:05.800
I've always been able to tell
when you're hiding something.

19:07.760 --> 19:09.240
People round here talk.

19:10.280 --> 19:12.320
Some of them work
at the BSA.

19:12.840 --> 19:15.400
I've been talking to wives
of factory hands.

19:15.480 --> 19:18.960
Detectives have been asking questions
in the proofing shops.

19:20.040 --> 19:23.640
Nothing happens in that factory
without you knowing about it.

19:24.480 --> 19:25.880
Speak.

19:26.440 --> 19:28.360
God and Aunt Polly
are listening.

19:38.720 --> 19:40.560
It was meant to be routine.

19:43.240 --> 19:46.760
I had a buyer in London
for some motorcycles.

19:47.320 --> 19:51.080
I asked my men to steal me
four bikes with petrol engines.

19:53.000 --> 19:55.320
I'm guessing my men were drunk.

19:55.800 --> 19:59.080
There's a still inside the factory
makes tram line gin. 

20:02.880 --> 20:05.480
They picked up
the wrong fucking crate. 

20:06.440 --> 20:09.640
The boys dropped it to Charlie Strong's
yard as agreed. 

20:10.160 --> 20:14.280
They must've taken it from the proofing
bay instead of the export bay. 

20:19.960 --> 20:22.520
Holy sweet baby of Mary.

20:22.600 --> 20:25.760
Inside we found
25 Lewis machine guns, 

20:25.960 --> 20:28.400
10,000 rounds of ammunition,

20:29.000 --> 20:30.920
50 semi-automatic rifles,

20:31.000 --> 20:33.200
200 pistols with shells.

20:33.280 --> 20:34.760
[Polly] Jesus, Tommy.

20:35.640 --> 20:37.400
All bound for Libya.

20:38.760 --> 20:41.360
Sitting right there
in Charlie Strong's yard.

20:44.440 --> 20:46.440
Tell me you threw
them in the Cut.

20:47.360 --> 20:49.840
We put them in the stables
out of the rain.

20:49.920 --> 20:52.040
The guns hadn't
been greased yet.

20:56.560 --> 20:59.320
So that's why they sent
a copper from Belfast.

20:59.760 --> 21:01.600
Maybe. Maybe not.

21:03.720 --> 21:05.640
Thomas, you're a bookmaker,

21:05.720 --> 21:08.360
a robber, a fighting man,
you are not a fool.

21:08.440 --> 21:12.280
You sell those guns to anyone
who has use for them, you will hang.

21:18.000 --> 21:20.600
Dump them somewhere
the police can find them.

21:20.680 --> 21:22.880
Maybe if they know
they haven't fallen

21:22.960 --> 21:25.440
into the wrong hands,
this might blow over.

21:25.880 --> 21:28.320
- Tell Charlie to dump them tonight.
- No.

21:29.000 --> 21:31.520
He won't move contraband
under a full moon.

21:31.760 --> 21:34.120
Three days until it wanes.

21:34.400 --> 21:36.280
Then you'll do the right thing?

21:39.120 --> 21:41.200
You have your mother's
common sense,

21:41.560 --> 21:43.240
but your father's devilment.

21:44.120 --> 21:45.560
I see them fighting.

21:46.720 --> 21:48.160
Let your mother win.

22:38.000 --> 22:39.960
I got tickets for
the Penny Crush.

22:40.040 --> 22:42.480
They're showing
a Tom Mix picture.

22:42.600 --> 22:45.000
I'm not in the mood
for pictures, Ada.

22:45.080 --> 22:47.040
Well, I'm not
doing it here again.

22:47.120 --> 22:48.920
I got covered in mud
last time.

22:49.000 --> 22:50.320
Let's just walk a bit.

22:50.400 --> 22:53.440
If we go down as far as Greet,
we could go to a pub.

22:53.520 --> 22:55.720
Your brothers have
friends in Greet.

22:55.800 --> 22:58.280
Everywhere.
We'd have to walk to London.

22:58.360 --> 23:01.320
You're the only man
around here not scared of them.

23:01.440 --> 23:03.880
Oh, I'm scared
of them all right.

23:03.960 --> 23:06.920
But you love me more than
you fear them, right?

23:08.200 --> 23:10.560
I don't want to be
always sneaking about.

23:11.400 --> 23:13.760
- Soon, we'll tell them.
- When?

23:18.120 --> 23:19.920
How did the family meeting go?

23:22.920 --> 23:24.040
Usual.

23:24.640 --> 23:27.000
- There's a new copper coming.
- I heard.

23:27.080 --> 23:30.480
Mmm. And Tommy says
he's after the likes of you.

23:30.560 --> 23:34.600
So maybe you should burn your books
and stop making speeches.

23:35.240 --> 23:37.120
Oh, my Ada.

23:37.200 --> 23:41.160
The only princess of the royal family
of the kingdom of Small Heath.

23:41.720 --> 23:44.520
I'm just a poor communist frog
with a big mouth.

23:48.680 --> 23:52.200
- Give me a kiss, Princess Ada.
- [giggles]

24:34.000 --> 24:36.320
I'm here about
the job as a barmaid.

24:39.080 --> 24:41.320
- Are you mad?
- Am I what?

24:41.400 --> 24:43.080
Do you know
about this place?

24:43.160 --> 24:45.240
I saw it in an advertisement.

24:45.320 --> 24:46.400
Job's been filled.

24:46.480 --> 24:48.320
But it was in
yesterday's paper.

24:48.400 --> 24:51.320
Believe me, love,
I'm doing you a favor.

24:51.400 --> 24:55.040
I'm not asking for favors,
I'm asking for employment.

24:57.680 --> 25:00.400
You're too... nice.

25:01.360 --> 25:03.560
- How would you know?
- Too pretty.

25:04.320 --> 25:06.320
They'd have you up
against a wall.

25:06.560 --> 25:08.040
I have experience.

25:08.440 --> 25:09.920
And references.

25:14.720 --> 25:16.680
What part of Ireland
are you from?

25:17.040 --> 25:18.680
- Galway.
- Ah.

25:19.480 --> 25:20.640
I worked in Dublin.

25:21.800 --> 25:23.480
My mother was from Galway.

25:26.920 --> 25:29.840
- You are too pretty.
- Watch.

25:30.840 --> 25:32.080
And listen.

25:34.200 --> 25:37.040
? I wish I was ? 

25:37.240 --> 25:41.080
? In Carrickfergus ? 

25:41.200 --> 25:43.520
? Only for nights ? 

25:43.600 --> 25:46.200
? In Ballygrand ? 

25:46.280 --> 25:49.840
? I would swim over ? 

25:49.920 --> 25:52.920
? The deepest ocean ? 

25:53.520 --> 25:55.680
? The deepest ocean ? 

25:55.760 --> 25:58.280
? For my love to find ? 

25:59.040 --> 26:02.160
? My boyhood friends ? 

26:02.240 --> 26:05.160
? And my own relations ? 

26:05.240 --> 26:08.000
? Have all passed on now ? 

26:08.080 --> 26:10.720
? Like the melting snow ? 

26:15.920 --> 26:20.160
In Ireland my singing made them cry
and stopped them fighting.

26:21.800 --> 26:23.680
I hope you know a lot of songs.

26:26.080 --> 26:28.680
[chattering]

27:13.120 --> 27:14.160
Babies.

27:15.680 --> 27:20.160
Discarded with the fish bones
and eggshells.

27:22.040 --> 27:23.320
Girls.

27:24.760 --> 27:26.400
11 years old.

27:27.800 --> 27:32.440
Pierced and punctured by old men
for three pence a time.

27:33.000 --> 27:35.280
Rutted upon like animals.

27:36.760 --> 27:38.360
Degradation.

27:39.320 --> 27:41.560
Fathers with their daughters,

27:41.640 --> 27:44.160
brothers and sisters
sharing beds.

27:44.920 --> 27:47.920
Beggars and thieves
left to run in the streets.

27:48.840 --> 27:54.560
And astride the whole stinking pile
of wounds and rotten flesh,

27:55.960 --> 27:57.480
your masters.

27:58.680 --> 28:01.520
The men who
you touch your cap to.

28:03.680 --> 28:05.600
The Peaky Blinders.

28:07.840 --> 28:11.080
The vicious, merciless gangs

28:11.880 --> 28:13.920
who blind those who see

28:14.480 --> 28:17.200
and cut out the tongues
of those who talk.

28:18.800 --> 28:21.120
You are worse than them.

28:24.320 --> 28:28.240
Those of you who have taken their bribes
these years since the war.

28:28.560 --> 28:31.560
Those of you who have
looked the other way,

28:31.760 --> 28:35.120
you are worse than them.

28:37.320 --> 28:40.680
God damn you for
soiling your uniforms!

28:44.200 --> 28:45.440
And then,

28:46.360 --> 28:48.320
there are t he IRA Fenians

28:49.480 --> 28:51.000
and the communists.

28:51.960 --> 28:53.880
Blacker hearts still.

28:54.640 --> 28:57.880
They feed on the puss
of all this corruption

28:58.400 --> 29:00.880
like maggots in a corpse!

29:02.160 --> 29:04.480
And like maggots
have left a swell

29:04.560 --> 29:07.440
they will eventually
swarm like flies

29:07.520 --> 29:10.200
and spread their
rotten philosophy

29:10.280 --> 29:13.240
across the country
and across the world.

29:13.640 --> 29:15.160
Those then...

29:16.560 --> 29:18.080
are our enemies.

29:19.760 --> 29:21.760
A three-headed beast.

29:21.880 --> 29:23.840
It is my job

29:23.920 --> 29:27.040
to decapitate each one,
and by God I will do it.

29:30.640 --> 29:33.440
I don't trust any of you

29:34.120 --> 29:36.720
until you earn my trust...

29:38.920 --> 29:40.920
and that takes some earning.

29:41.000 --> 29:42.120
[door opens]

29:45.200 --> 29:49.000
These are the new men
who will bolster your ranks.

29:51.040 --> 29:55.000
Good men
from God-fearing families.

29:57.280 --> 29:59.720
By the time the sun sets,

29:59.840 --> 30:02.280
they will be sworn in
and in uniform.

30:02.360 --> 30:04.360
And by sunrise tomorrow,

30:04.440 --> 30:06.280
they will be on the streets.

30:10.160 --> 30:13.040
God help those
who stand in our way.

30:18.000 --> 30:19.600
[woman] Sorry, Mr. Shelby.

30:19.800 --> 30:22.400
- Right.
- Get out of the way for Mr. Shelby.

30:22.480 --> 30:24.840
- [man] Mr. Shelby.
- [Arthur] This way.

30:26.680 --> 30:28.240
You see, ladies?

30:28.320 --> 30:30.160
When you're out with a Blinder,

30:30.240 --> 30:31.760
you don't have to queue.

30:36.040 --> 30:39.480
Right, I want a blow job
off both of you

30:39.560 --> 30:41.800
before they let the ordinary
people in.

30:41.880 --> 30:44.120
Away you go.
Take it out.

30:44.200 --> 30:45.440
What the fuck?

30:46.160 --> 30:48.320
Who the fuck are you?

30:48.880 --> 30:51.080
I am Arthur fucking Shelby!

30:51.160 --> 30:54.720
- [punches thudding]
- [Arthur groaning]

31:14.320 --> 31:15.800
[Campbell] Arthur Shelby.

31:16.280 --> 31:18.080
Lead pack dog

31:18.400 --> 31:20.360
of the Peaky Blinders.

31:32.000 --> 31:33.360
Look at me.

31:45.600 --> 31:47.040
[grunts, coughs]

31:47.680 --> 31:48.680
[groans]

31:56.120 --> 31:57.400
[Arthur] Bastard!

32:01.360 --> 32:02.800
[Campbell] Your uniform?

32:03.560 --> 32:05.240
Terrifying, I'm sure.

32:06.480 --> 32:08.720
- Did he have a gun?
- [Moss] No gun.

32:08.800 --> 32:11.160
Knife in his sock.
Cosh in his belt.

32:16.000 --> 32:17.520
Now, Mr. Shelby...

32:19.320 --> 32:23.760
I want you to see this
as me introducing myself to you.

32:24.280 --> 32:25.520
Understand?

32:26.440 --> 32:28.160
In all the world,

32:28.240 --> 32:32.000
the only thing that
interests me is the truth.

32:33.280 --> 32:34.440
So...

32:36.800 --> 32:38.800
What do you know
about the robbery?

32:39.840 --> 32:40.960
What robbery?

32:43.600 --> 32:46.040
[breathing heavily]

32:50.320 --> 32:51.920
I will ask you again.

32:53.480 --> 32:56.760
What do you know
about the robbery?

32:56.840 --> 32:58.320
I swear to God,

32:58.400 --> 33:00.680
I don't know what
you're talking about.

33:00.760 --> 33:02.880
What fucking robbery?

33:04.160 --> 33:06.720
- [snap]
- [screaming]

33:07.840 --> 33:09.320
[groaning]

33:14.360 --> 33:18.200
After 35 years of
dealing with animals like you,

33:18.520 --> 33:21.600
I can tell just by
sniffing the air

33:21.760 --> 33:23.520
whether or not you are lying.

33:25.240 --> 33:27.800
I'm not fucking lying!
All right?

33:27.880 --> 33:29.400
I'm not fucking lying.

33:38.240 --> 33:39.280
I know.

33:44.280 --> 33:47.520
I see nothing of interest
behind the blood in your eyes.

33:48.800 --> 33:51.400
And no blood in your veins
that could carry

33:52.280 --> 33:55.880
even a trace
of cunning or guile.

33:57.800 --> 33:59.360
But understand this.

34:01.560 --> 34:03.840
It is well within my power

34:04.680 --> 34:07.760
to have you and the rest
of your scum family

34:08.639 --> 34:11.719
face down in the canal
before the year is out.

34:15.239 --> 34:16.920
On the other hand...

34:20.600 --> 34:22.159
we can help each other.

34:29.159 --> 34:31.120
[chatter, laughter]

34:36.080 --> 34:38.679
[Grace] Is it always
this busy on a daytime?

34:38.760 --> 34:41.480
No. These boys are on
their way to St. Andrews.

34:41.600 --> 34:43.400
- Pray?
- That'll be the day!

34:43.480 --> 34:46.760
St. Andrews is a football ground.
The Blues are playing.

34:46.840 --> 34:51.000
That's the forward line there
and that's the goalie, believe it or not.

34:51.080 --> 34:52.239
[Thomas] Hello!

34:56.880 --> 34:58.280
I need a bottle of rum.

34:58.360 --> 35:00.720
Grace? Whatever it is,
it's on the house.

35:00.800 --> 35:02.280
- A whole bottle?
- Yeah.

35:02.360 --> 35:04.320
- White or dark rum?
- Don't care.

35:04.400 --> 35:06.840
[Harry] Right, lads,
what will it be, two?

35:08.000 --> 35:09.080
Thank you.

35:11.560 --> 35:13.280
Harry said it's on the house.

35:15.400 --> 35:16.600
Are you a whore?

35:20.600 --> 35:23.440
Because if you're not,
you're in the wrong place.

35:29.640 --> 35:31.800
He's one of them
you warned me about.

35:31.880 --> 35:34.880
Grace, you're a friendly girl,
but be careful.

35:34.960 --> 35:36.920
If I say something's
on the house,

35:37.000 --> 35:39.480
then say nothing to whoever
you're serving.

35:39.560 --> 35:44.000
If they decide that they want you
there's nothing anybody could do about it.

35:44.080 --> 35:46.720
Lucky for you, since
he got back from France,

35:46.800 --> 35:49.680
Tommy doesn't want
anybody at all. Yes, lads?

35:50.120 --> 35:52.560
[grunting]

35:52.680 --> 35:55.720
- Wipe the blood out of his eye.
- You give orders?

35:55.800 --> 35:57.040
I'm a trained nurse.

35:57.120 --> 35:59.320
Don't make me laugh,
it hurts my face.

35:59.400 --> 36:00.880
[Ada] I bloody am.

36:00.960 --> 36:03.520
You went to one
class in the church hall

36:03.600 --> 36:05.480
and got thrown out
for giggling.

36:05.560 --> 36:07.760
Not before I learned
to stop choking.

36:07.840 --> 36:09.800
I'm not bloody
choking, am I?

36:09.920 --> 36:13.000
You will be when I wrap
this cloth round your neck.

36:13.120 --> 36:16.480
Let me see him. Well, have this.

36:19.720 --> 36:20.800
Give me that.

36:25.760 --> 36:27.000
You're all right.

36:29.200 --> 36:31.880
He said Mr. Churchill
sent him to Birmingham.

36:33.440 --> 36:35.160
National interest, he said.

36:35.720 --> 36:37.400
Something about a robbery.

36:41.240 --> 36:43.080
He said he wants us
to help him.

36:43.160 --> 36:44.480
We don't help coppers.

36:44.560 --> 36:46.600
He knew all about
our war records.

36:47.600 --> 36:50.800
He said we're patriots like him.

36:51.880 --> 36:54.880
He wants us to be
his eyes and ears.

36:56.800 --> 36:58.080
I said...

37:00.360 --> 37:05.000
I said we'd have a family
meeting and take a vote.

37:12.480 --> 37:14.440
Well, why not? Mmm?

37:15.120 --> 37:18.200
We have no truck with
Fenians or communists.

37:23.440 --> 37:24.880
What's wrong with you?

37:26.240 --> 37:28.680
What the fuck is wrong
with him lately?

37:28.760 --> 37:31.760
If I knew, I'd buy the cure
from Compton's chemists.

37:33.480 --> 37:36.600
? I am just a young girl ? 

37:36.680 --> 37:39.400
? I have just come over ? 

37:39.480 --> 37:41.880
? Over from the country ? 

37:41.960 --> 37:45.080
? Where they do things big ? 

37:45.520 --> 37:48.200
? And amongst the boys ? 

37:48.280 --> 37:51.880
? I have got myself a lover ? 

37:51.960 --> 37:55.640
? And since I have a lover ? 

37:55.720 --> 37:58.960
? I don't care a thing ? 

37:59.040 --> 38:04.840
? The boy I love is
up in the gallery ? 

38:04.920 --> 38:08.880
? The boy I love
is looking at me ? 

38:08.960 --> 38:10.400
[crowd quiets]

38:10.480 --> 38:13.480
[Grace] ? Can't you see him
standing there? ? 

38:13.560 --> 38:16.840
? Waving his handkerchief ? 

38:16.920 --> 38:20.360
? As merry as a robin ? 

38:20.440 --> 38:23.040
? That sings on the tree ? 

38:31.360 --> 38:33.960
We haven't had singing
in here since the war.

38:35.280 --> 38:37.160
Why do you think
that is, Harry?

38:40.560 --> 38:42.000
[groaning]

38:42.720 --> 38:44.400
[moaning]

39:10.840 --> 39:12.440
So did Arthur say...

39:14.280 --> 39:17.080
what kind of a deal
this new copper offered him?

39:17.160 --> 39:21.240
God. The second your balls are empty,
it's back onto politics.

39:29.760 --> 39:31.080
What did Tommy say?

39:31.160 --> 39:33.960
He didn't say anything.
You know what he's like.

39:34.040 --> 39:35.640
Yeah, I know
what he's like.

39:35.720 --> 39:38.080
He likes to take his fights
onto the mud.

39:38.160 --> 39:40.080
Doesn't like to
stand and wait.

39:40.160 --> 39:42.920
You know what he'd do
if he found out about us.

39:43.000 --> 39:43.960
He could try.

39:44.040 --> 39:47.280
Sometimes it's like you're with me
just to show you can.

39:51.240 --> 39:54.240
One day me and Tommy
will be on the same side again.

41:15.040 --> 41:16.560
[Danny] Tommy!

41:16.640 --> 41:18.600
[screaming]

41:18.680 --> 41:19.720
[Thomas] Danny!

41:20.920 --> 41:22.560
[screaming]

41:23.240 --> 41:24.280
Danny!

41:24.360 --> 41:25.760
[gasping]

41:26.200 --> 41:29.080
[deep breathing]

42:03.560 --> 42:06.680
[whimpering]

42:16.880 --> 42:19.560
Hey, what you do?
We're closed.

42:20.400 --> 42:21.560
Go home!

42:22.760 --> 42:26.320
Go home, crazy man.
I said, go home, crazy man!

42:27.640 --> 42:29.840
- [speaks Italian]
- [babbling]

42:30.000 --> 42:33.160
- I said, go home.
- Fix bayonets!

42:34.000 --> 42:36.960
[children screaming]

42:38.880 --> 42:41.440
[people chattering]

43:07.840 --> 43:10.960
Secretary of State, this is
Chief Inspector Campbell.

43:16.280 --> 43:17.720
Mr. Churchill, sir.

43:18.520 --> 43:21.320
May I say what a great honor
it is to meet you.

43:21.400 --> 43:23.840
Bit of a whistle stop tour.

43:23.920 --> 43:26.000
Love the hat, by the way.

43:26.080 --> 43:27.160
Thank you.

43:28.440 --> 43:29.720
It's beaver.

43:31.360 --> 43:33.640
So, how are you settling in?

43:35.000 --> 43:36.840
I have set up
a command network.

43:36.920 --> 43:39.360
I have agents in place
across the city

43:39.440 --> 43:41.400
who will act as
my eyes and ears.

43:42.360 --> 43:46.360
And I have begun to interrogate
suspects vigorously.

43:47.640 --> 43:49.480
You were in Belfast.

43:49.800 --> 43:52.840
I understand you broke
a few Fenian hearts.

43:54.160 --> 43:55.440
A rat's nest, sir.

43:55.520 --> 43:57.840
So who do you think
stole the guns?

43:57.920 --> 44:01.920
- The Fenians or the communists?
- If it is the IRA Fenians,

44:02.440 --> 44:04.960
I will find them
and find the guns.

44:05.040 --> 44:08.320
If it is communists,
I will find them and find the guns.

44:08.400 --> 44:12.080
If it is common criminals,
I will find them and find the guns.

44:12.920 --> 44:16.080
To me there is no distinction
between any of the above.

44:17.280 --> 44:20.240
Ah. We chose you
because you are effective,

44:20.320 --> 44:22.560
but remember this, Mr. Campbell,

44:22.640 --> 44:24.960
this is England, not Belfast.

44:25.040 --> 44:28.560
Bodies thrown in the rivers
wash up in the papers here.

44:28.720 --> 44:32.640
We must keep the existence
of these stolen guns out of the news,

44:32.720 --> 44:35.680
otherwise we're simply
advertising them for sale.

44:36.320 --> 44:38.800
If there are bodies
to be buried,

44:39.760 --> 44:40.920
dig holes,

44:41.920 --> 44:43.400
and dig them deep.

44:45.240 --> 44:47.160
I want everything
accounted for,

44:47.240 --> 44:48.960
down to the last bullet.

45:02.720 --> 45:05.160
[Thomas] Uncle Charlie, a word.

45:06.080 --> 45:09.240
They are aboard.
There's no moon.

45:09.640 --> 45:12.000
We can take them out
to the turning point

45:12.080 --> 45:14.720
beyond Gas Street
and leave them on the bank.

45:14.800 --> 45:17.360
They'll be found by
railway men first thing.

45:23.840 --> 45:25.520
Is that agreement?

45:28.080 --> 45:29.880
I changed my mind.

45:30.840 --> 45:32.120
You what?

45:34.120 --> 45:36.000
I have an alternative strategy.

45:38.040 --> 45:41.080
Tell Curly to take her out
to the old tobacco wharf.

45:41.160 --> 45:44.240
There's a lock-up mooring
we used to keep cigarettes.

45:44.320 --> 45:45.480
He knows it.

45:46.160 --> 45:50.000
When the boat leaves your yard,
it's no longer your concern.

45:52.040 --> 45:54.040
Have you lost
your fucking mind?

45:54.720 --> 45:56.520
Have you not seen the streets?

45:56.600 --> 45:59.440
They've sent a fucking army
to find these things.

45:59.520 --> 46:02.320
That's right. They've shown their hand.

46:02.400 --> 46:03.440
Their hand?

46:03.520 --> 46:06.640
If they want them back this bad,
they'll have to pay.

46:06.720 --> 46:08.400
That's the way of the world.

46:08.480 --> 46:11.240
Fortune drops something
valuable into your lap,

46:11.320 --> 46:13.800
you don't dump it
on the bank of the Cut.

46:16.320 --> 46:17.760
You're blood, Tommy.

46:19.040 --> 46:21.480
I've always looked out
for you like a dad.

46:24.040 --> 46:27.000
You're going to bring holy hell
down on your head.

46:28.520 --> 46:30.920
This copper
takes no prisoners.

46:31.920 --> 46:33.840
I'm told he didn't serve.

46:34.920 --> 46:36.560
Reserved occupation.

46:39.800 --> 46:42.360
Is it another war
you're looking for, Tommy?

46:43.640 --> 46:45.400
The tobacco wharf.

46:46.800 --> 46:48.920
By order of the Peaky Blinders.

47:20.480 --> 47:22.120
Are you in position?

47:25.040 --> 47:26.400
I am, sir.

47:28.040 --> 47:30.080
Your first impressions.

47:30.600 --> 47:33.160
I am quite shocked
at how these people live.

47:36.080 --> 47:38.800
Have you found anything out
that might help me?

47:38.880 --> 47:41.600
I interrogated the head
of the Peaky Blinders.

47:41.680 --> 47:43.320
He didn't know anything.

47:43.400 --> 47:44.560
A brute.

47:44.960 --> 47:48.640
It strikes me that it isn't Arthur
who heads the Shelby family.

47:48.720 --> 47:50.120
It is the younger one,

47:50.520 --> 47:51.640
Thomas.

47:53.960 --> 47:56.960
They say he won two medals
for gallantry in the war.

47:57.560 --> 47:59.200
You sound fascinated.

48:01.960 --> 48:05.040
However, my opinion
has not changed.

48:05.520 --> 48:07.760
The bookmaker gangs
have other business

48:07.840 --> 48:10.920
and the communists are too weak
to have planned this.

48:12.520 --> 48:15.160
I believe the guns were
taken by the IRA.

48:17.400 --> 48:20.120
You must not let your personal history

48:20.640 --> 48:22.000
cloud your judgment.

48:26.480 --> 48:28.000
What history?

48:30.000 --> 48:34.200
That the IRA murdered my father
will not affect my judgment.

48:38.360 --> 48:39.720
If you see any guns,

48:40.960 --> 48:43.480
check the serial numbers
against that list.

48:47.400 --> 48:48.720
Your father

48:49.200 --> 48:52.080
was the finest officer
I ever worked with.

48:52.840 --> 48:55.520
I know he'd be very,
very proud of you.

49:25.120 --> 49:28.440
Danny, as you know,
the man you killed was Italian.

49:30.120 --> 49:32.800
And those two men over there
are his brothers.

49:35.880 --> 49:38.000
If I let the Italians
do this, Danny,

49:38.920 --> 49:41.640
they'll cut off your manhood
and let you drain.

49:42.440 --> 49:44.960
That's how those
bastards do things.

49:46.320 --> 49:49.760
So, to stop a war breaking out
between us and the Italians,

49:51.880 --> 49:54.320
and to save you
from their barbarity...

49:57.280 --> 49:59.520
I said I would dispatch you myself.

50:01.800 --> 50:03.320
They are here to witness.

50:11.000 --> 50:13.000
I died over there anyway, Tommy.

50:14.720 --> 50:16.840
I left my fucking
brains in the mud.

50:20.640 --> 50:22.720
You have any last
requests, comrade?

50:28.440 --> 50:31.680
You'll look out for
my Rosie and my boys.

50:34.360 --> 50:36.080
See they get apprenticeships.

50:36.400 --> 50:39.320
At the BSA factory or the Austin.

50:42.240 --> 50:44.840
And they'll make foremen.
I know they will.

50:46.360 --> 50:48.440
Just ordinary.

50:49.640 --> 50:51.600
Just ordinary men.

50:51.920 --> 50:54.160
And they won't get told
to do the shit,

50:55.080 --> 50:58.200
the shit, the shit
that we got told to do.

51:00.320 --> 51:02.480
[whimpering]

51:10.920 --> 51:12.920
I suppose I ought to pray now.

51:16.680 --> 51:18.160
Those fucking guns,

51:18.240 --> 51:21.320
they blew God right out of my head.

51:28.000 --> 51:29.360
Is that boat for me?

51:33.680 --> 51:36.560
We have to get your body
out of the city, Danny.

51:36.640 --> 51:38.320
This new copper, you know...

51:38.400 --> 51:41.200
Don't bury me anywhere
there's mud. Okay?

51:42.280 --> 51:43.480
Promise me.

51:46.160 --> 51:47.360
Bury me on a hill.

51:48.120 --> 51:49.560
And tell Rosie where.

51:53.560 --> 51:54.960
You were a good man

51:56.160 --> 51:57.520
and a good soldier.

52:01.520 --> 52:03.160
Yes, Sergeant Major.

52:20.560 --> 52:21.920
[cocks gun]

52:25.120 --> 52:27.160
In the bleak midwinter.

52:45.080 --> 52:46.520
[gunshot]

53:16.520 --> 53:18.040
[Arthur] Where are you?

53:21.880 --> 53:23.440
It bloody won!

53:23.760 --> 53:26.160
Monaghan Boy bloody won!

53:27.640 --> 53:29.760
Yeah. It won.

53:31.520 --> 53:33.040
And word will spread.

53:33.160 --> 53:35.520
So the next time
we do the powder trick,

53:35.600 --> 53:38.800
it won't just be the Garrison
that'll bet on the horse,

53:38.880 --> 53:41.960
it'll be the whole of Small Heath.
And you know what?

53:42.800 --> 53:44.280
The horse will win again.

53:44.360 --> 53:46.000
And the third time
we do it,

53:46.080 --> 53:48.960
we'll have the whole
of Birmingham betting on it.

53:49.040 --> 53:51.840
1,000-quid bet on
the magic horse.

53:51.920 --> 53:53.240
And that time,

53:54.320 --> 53:55.560
when we are ready,

53:56.160 --> 53:57.600
the horse will lose.

54:01.640 --> 54:02.840
Think about it.

54:41.800 --> 54:43.360
[Charlie] You okay, Danny?

54:43.440 --> 54:44.960
I'm still in shock.

54:46.960 --> 54:49.040
Are you sure
this isn't heaven?

54:49.120 --> 54:51.720
If it was heaven,
what would I be doing here?

54:54.800 --> 54:57.000
Tommy wanted you
to think it was real,

54:57.200 --> 54:59.320
to try and knock
some sense into you.

54:59.640 --> 55:02.320
A shell full of sheep brains
hurts pretty bad.

55:02.400 --> 55:03.640
Ah, it was meant to.

55:06.040 --> 55:07.640
So where are you taking me?

55:07.720 --> 55:10.560
London. Tommy has a little job for you.

55:10.920 --> 55:12.840
Give you a chance to say thanks.

55:17.280 --> 55:19.320
You're a Peaky Blinder now, Danny.

55:32.800 --> 55:34.320
[Polly] A bad week.

55:36.160 --> 55:37.840
There was no moon
last night.

55:38.520 --> 55:39.520
I checked.

55:39.600 --> 55:43.080
- Did you do the right thing?
- Yes. I did the right thing.

56:26.080 --> 56:31.120
[theme song playing]
